---
/* The visual is a photograph of two hands cupping warm light on black.

   It replaces a cloudscape, and the swap is the point: the section says calm
   should be standard care, and a sky says calm without saying care. Hands
   holding a light say both, and they do it without a stock clinician in a
   corridor — which would have said neither and looked like filler.

   Shot on near-black, so it screens into this section the way the hero subject
   screens into the top of the page rather than sitting in a box on top of it.
   See public/assets/photos/CREDITS.md. */
---

<section class="manifesto" data-color-scheme="dark" aria-labelledby="manifesto-heading">
  <div class="container page-section manifesto__inner">
    <picture class="manifesto__visual">
      <source srcset="/assets/photos/hands@1x.webp 1x, /assets/photos/hands.webp 2x" type="image/webp" />
      <img src="/assets/photos/hands.webp" alt="" width="1600" height="1067" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </picture>

    <div class="manifesto__copy">
      <h2 id="manifesto-heading" class="manifesto__heading">Calm should be standard care.</h2>
      <p class="manifesto__body">
        Emergency rooms feel chaotic because nobody can see what is coming. Patients wait in the
        dark, and care teams meet every story cold. When the story arrives first, the waiting room
        finally makes sense to <em>both</em> of them.
      </p>
      <a class="manifesto__cta" href="/product">See the product</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .manifesto {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    /* Not flat slate. The same two lights the hero uses, at a fraction of the
       strength, so the one dark section on the page belongs to the same world
       as the top of it rather than being a grey box in the middle. */
    background-color: var(--slate-90);
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 68% 60% at 12% 8%, rgb(from var(--solace-60) r g b / 0.24), transparent 66%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 72% 64% at 92% 96%, rgb(from var(--solace-90) r g b / 0.44), transparent 70%);
    color: var(--color-text-base);
  }

  .manifesto__inner { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-10x); }
  @media (min-width: 1080.02px) {
    .manifesto__inner { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-16x); }
    .manifesto__inner > * { flex: 1 1 0; min-inline-size: 0; }
    /* Image left, copy right, matching the reference. The visual is already
       first in the DOM, so no order override is needed; the previous
       :last-child{order:-1} was flipping it the wrong way. */
  }

  /* Same graded sky pipeline as the hero, so the two plates read as one
     world. Replaces the CSS-only fallback, which was three overlapping blurs
     and looked like a placeholder next to a photographic hero. */
  /* No frame and no shadow. The plate is on black, so a radius and a box
     shadow would draw a rectangle around something that has no edges — the
     mask lets it dissolve into the section instead. */
  /* Screened, not framed. The plate is shot on near-black, so screen takes its
     background to nothing for free and the hands appear to be lit BY the
     section rather than pasted into it — the same compositing the hero uses on
     its subject, which is why the two now read as one world.

     The mask has to reach transparent well before the edges or the rectangle
     survives. At 42%/100% the top edge was still around half opacity and the
     straight line was plainly visible. */
  .manifesto__visual {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    mix-blend-mode: screen;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 78% 76% at 48% 52%, #000 18%, transparent 76%);
            mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 78% 76% at 48% 52%, #000 18%, transparent 76%);
  }
  .manifesto__visual img { display: block; inline-size: 100%; }

  /* Parallax, bound to the section's own travel rather than a clock, so it
     tracks the scroll in both directions. A still plate in a box was the one
     thing on the page that did not respond to being scrolled past at all. */
  /* A real move, not a nudge. It arrives pushed down and oversized and settles
     as the section crosses — big enough to notice, slow enough not to shout. */
  @keyframes manifesto-drift {
    from { scale: 1.26; translate: 0 7%; }
    to   { scale: 1.04; translate: 0 -4%; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
      .manifesto__visual img {
        animation: manifesto-drift linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: cover 0% cover 100%;
      }
    }
  }
  .manifesto__visual img {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1080 / 888;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .manifesto__copy { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-6x); }

  .manifesto__heading {
    font-size: var(--font-size-32);
    line-height: 96%;
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-display);
  }
  @media (min-width: 640.02px)  { .manifesto__heading { font-size: var(--font-size-36); } }
  @media (min-width: 1080.02px) { .manifesto__heading { font-size: var(--font-size-48); } }

  .manifesto__body {
    font-size: var(--font-size-text-medium);
    color: var(--color-text-sub);
    max-inline-size: 54ch;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1080.02px) { .manifesto__body { font-size: var(--font-size-20); } }
  .manifesto__body em { font-style: italic; color: var(--color-text-base); }

  .manifesto__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-3x) var(--space-6x);
    border-radius: var(--radius-3x);
    border: 1px solid rgb(from var(--white) r g b / 0.32);
    font-size: var(--font-size-16);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: normal;
    transition: background-color var(--motion-duration-base) var(--ease-ui),
                border-color var(--motion-duration-base) var(--ease-ui);
  }
  .manifesto__cta:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-transparent-hover);
    border-color: rgb(from var(--white) r g b / 0.55);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .manifesto__cta { transition: none; } }
</style>
